|~ What is declared under `::desc`, the kind of a value whose place
   in the one order is the reverse of its payload's: its comparisons,
   which compare two of its values by their payloads, reversed. ~|

:desc/gt
  |~~ Whether the subject follows the value the call gives among
      descending values, which holds when its payload precedes the
      other's.

      ~(1 | desc | gt (2 | desc) | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:desc/gt/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:desc/gt/than/NotDescError |~~ The than is a value of ::desc. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::desc)

:desc/gt/greater |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:desc/gte
  |~~ Whether the subject follows or equals the value the call gives
      among descending values.

      ~(2 | desc | gte (2 | desc) | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:desc/gte/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:desc/gte/than/NotDescError |~~ The than is a value of ::desc. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::desc)

:desc/gte/atLeast |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:desc/lt
  |~~ Whether the subject precedes the value the call gives among
      descending values, which holds when its payload follows the
      other's.

      ~(2 | desc | lt (1 | desc) | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:desc/lt/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:desc/lt/than/NotDescError |~~ The than is a value of ::desc. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::desc)

:desc/lt/less |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:desc/lte
  |~~ Whether the subject precedes or equals the value the call gives
      among descending values.

      ~(2 | desc | lte (2 | desc) | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:desc/lte/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:desc/lte/than/NotDescError |~~ The than is a value of ::desc. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::desc)

:desc/lte/atMost |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean
